# Jeux and JEUX Romantiques information
#
# Created by Andrew Purdam, and converted as an attachment to test the
# nwc2beta newsgroup's ability to receive nwcitree attachments.
#
# Comments from Adrew:
# 
# Here is an instrument tree for the Jeux and JEUX Romantiques soundfont
# (normally banks 42 & 43). You will note that the itree predefines the
# soundbank information for you, which is pretty neat.
# 
# HTH,
# A
# Jeux d'orgues information 
#
# submitted by jan J.H.Hofland
#
# Stefan's pipe organ information - submitted by - I forget
#
# This file will give you the nwcitree for "Stefan's Cathedral Pipe Organ" soundfont,
# which is available from Hammersound.
# Once it is DL'd and unzipped, however, you will still need to un-PACK it,
# using SFPack (Google it!)
#
#
# Percussion courtesy of Tina Billett July 2005
#
#
# Roland Edirol Orchestral added by Stuart Moffatt May 2005
#
# Installation:
#
# Backup your native "default.nwcitree" file and copy
# this file to your "\Noteworthy Composer 2\itrees" folder
# if you wish to use it as your default instrument tree.
#
# If you wish to keep your default i-tree, rename this file
# and copy it to the mentioned directory.
#
# See additional notes at the end taken from Sample.nwcitree
#
# Organisation of the file:

\General MIDI
\General User GS
\sYnerGi v1
\Organs
\Yamaha XG
\Roland GS
\MT-32

